# Workspace structure

## Source of truth

- `stackrox/` is the main product UI clone (`github.com/stackrox/stackrox`).
- Prefer designing and exploring against the **local live UI** in `stackrox/ui/` with staging (`UI_START_TARGET` + `ROX_API_TOKEN` from `.secrets/`).
- Do not treat feature prototype folders as the product SoT.

## Feature subfolders

- Each effort lives in a top-level folder (e.g. `risk-lightspeed/`) built off the current `stackrox/` UI.
- These folders are static click-through prototypes (MSW + in-repo mock JSON) meant for GitHub Pages share links.
- Support multiple versions (baseline / v1 / v2…) with a switcher and `?prototype=` links so eng feedback can iterate without destroying prior options.
- Pages URL: `https://mansursyed.github.io/rhacs-ux-prototypes/<feature>/`

## Lifecycle

1. Pull / refresh `stackrox/` from upstream.
2. Work live against staging in `stackrox/`.
3. Branch a feature prototype folder for shareable review.
4. When the real change ships upstream, pull latest into `stackrox/` and base future work on that.
